34,0 $ Pileus chestnut brown, chestnut purplish or date brown, then rusty tawny, brick or purplish date, radially fibrillose; stipe white to concolorous with pileus; spores 8.0-10 (11) x 4.0-5.0 (6.0) µm , ellipsoid to lacrimoid; cheilocystidia scattered to rather fréquent; on soil in grassy anthropogenous places $ G. potassiovirescens
35,0 $  (31) Basidiocarps reminiscent of Marasmius oreades with fairly pale yellowish to ochre- brown colours and pruinose stipe, which may become almost glabrous with âge $ G. oreadoides
