38,0 $  (37) Pileus yellow-brown or reddish brown, paler at margin, pallescent with âge to pinkish Isabella or pinkish-yellow; stipe orange-brown to red-brown, sometimes paler at apex, dark red-brown towards base, glabrous when very young, then covered with fine, white or yellow hairs, with strigose base; incrustation not turning green in alkalis; on litter of Fagus, in pure Fagus-woods or in mixed stands $ G. fagiphilus
38,39 $ Pileus chestnut-brown or purplish-brown when moist, pallescent to pallid brown or cream or brown at centre and paler (pale cream, beige or whitish) at margin; stipe whitish to pale cream when young, becoming brown to concolorous with pileus, entirely pubescent, densely tomentose towards base; incrustation turning green in alkalis; saprotrophic on végétal débris (leaves, branches), especially of Quercus or Pinus, in mixed stands, sometimes under Juniperus, or on fallen Quercus-leaves, rarely on leaves of other broad- leaved trees
39,0 $  (38) Pileus 10-40 mm brown, chestnut-brown or purplish-brown when moist, pallescent to pallid brown or cream on drying; lamellae pale cream to buff; stipe becoming concolorous with pileus with âge; on végétal débris (leaves, branches), especially of Quercus or Pinus, or in mixed stands, sometimes under Juniperus, in thermophilic forests on calcareous soils $G. pubipes var. pubipes
39,0 $ Pileus smaller, 15-30 mm broad, with brown centre and paler (pale cream, beige or whitish) margin; lamellae paler; stipe paler, almost whitish above and brown towards base; on fallen Quercus-leaves, rarely on leaves of other broad-leaved trees (Acer campestre, Carpinus) $G. pubipes var. pallidopileatus
